# Line endings, normalized in the repository (#310).
#
# Without this, a contributor on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites the line endings of
# every file they touch, and a one-line change arrives as a whole-file diff. Normalizing here
# makes the rule a property of the repository rather than of each clone's local git config.
#
# `text=auto` stores text as LF and lets git decide per file what is text; the explicit rules
# below cover the cases where guessing wrong is expensive.
* text=auto

# Project files are written by the application as JSON with \n, and the whole point of the
# format is that a saved graph diffs cleanly and reviewably. A checkout that turned them into
# CRLF would make every line differ the first time the app rewrote one on another platform, so
# these are pinned to LF in the working tree too, not merely in the repository.
*.ymir text eol=lf
*.ymirsub text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and the git hook run under Git Bash on Windows, which needs LF: a CRLF shebang
# line makes the interpreter lookup fail with a message that names a command that looks correct.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Shaders are compiled from source strings embedded at build time. Nothing depends on their
# line endings, but keeping them LF means a shader diff stays readable next to the Rust that
# includes it.
*.wgsl text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never attempts line-ending conversion or a textual merge on them.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary

# Third-party bytes, left exactly as their authors shipped them.
#
# `vendor/egui-snarl` is upstream source, which uses CRLF, and `patches/` holds unified diffs
# taken against that pristine source; patches/README.md states that applying them in order
# reproduces the vendored tree exactly. Normalizing either would break that on the next upgrade,
# for no benefit: nobody edits the vendored tree by hand. OFL.txt is the font licence as IBM
# published it, redistributed verbatim.
vendor/** -text
patches/*.patch -text
crates/ymir-gui/assets/fonts/OFL.txt -text

# The node reference under docs/reference/nodes/ is generated by `cargo xtask docs-gen` from each
# node's NodeSpec and prose fragment. Marking it linguist-generated collapses it in diffs and keeps
# it out of GitHub's language statistics. Edit the fragments in crates/ymir-nodes/docs/, not these.
docs/reference/nodes/*.md linguist-generated=true
